tate":"range","requirement":"required","min":235,"max":255,"verdict":"within"},"bed":{"text":"90–110 °C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":90,"max":110,"verdict":"within"},"chamber":{"state":"unknown","verdict":"unknown"},"plate":"Magigoo PA, PVA glue","notes":[{"topic":"Speed","text":"of printing 30–50 mm/s"}]},{"id":"P1380","product":"G154-01","source":"R-FILLAMENTUM-PRIORITY-20261003-3f22b7dd7442","kind":"Manufacturer published guidance","at":"p. 2: p.2 Table1 own product row NYLON AF80 ARAMID; own minimum-time/temperature/need columns, with p1 restrictions","nozzle":{"state":"unknown","verdict":"unknown"},"bed":{"state":"unknown","verdict":"unknown"},"chamber":{"state":"unknown","verdict":"unknown"},"drying":{"text":"80 °C; minimum drying time 4 h; the need to dry 5 (1 – not necessary to dry, 5 – always needed)","state":"stated","need":"required","c":[null,80],"h":[null,4],"hoursOpen":true},"notes":[{"topic":"Failure modes","text":"The filament must be dried in the device with exact thermoregulation (ideally laboratory dryer) – before drying the whole spool, put a little piece of filament into the device for the test of functionality. If the material becomes softer or loses its original shape, lower the drying temperature. In the case of loss of transparency, use a different device. The spool can’t be put into the environment without a controlled value of relative humidity after drying. The cooling process must be taken in the desiccator (or in the sealing box with the content of silica gel). If the hot spool is placed into an environment with higher humidity, the moisture may be absorbed back in about 10 minutes. And possibly on a higher level of moisture than it was before drying! The coil should not be left in the dryer after it has been switched off, as there is still evaporated moisture in the environment which can be absorbed back into the filament in the same way. For Nylon materials, the drying temperature must not exceed 80 °C, otherwise, oxo-degradation of the polymer will occur."}]},{"id":"P1394","product":"G154-01","source":"R-FILLAMENTUM-READER-20261004-119857e63f29","kind":"Manufacturer published guidance","at":"p. 1: Printing guide","nozzle":{"text":"235 – 255 °C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":235,"max":255,"verdict":"within"},"bed":{"text":"90 – 110 °C","state":"range","requirement":"required","min":90,"max":110,"verdict":"within"},"chamber":{"text":"recommended","state":"recommended","requirement":"recommended","verdict":"unknown"},"enclosure":{"text":"Heated chamber / enclosure: recommended","state":"recommended"},"drying":{"text":"In case of moist material, re-dry it in appropriate drying device; 80 °C for 3 hours","state":"stated","need":"optional","c":[null,80],"h":[null,3],"hoursOpen":false},"abrasion":"It is recommended to use wear-resistant nozzles (hardened steel, ruby, Dexdo nozzle etc.) due to the content of aramid fibers","hardened":true,"plate":"PEI, mirror / glass","notes":[{"topic":"Speed","text":"30 – 50 mm/s"},{"topic":"Cooling","text":"0 %"},{"topic":"Adhesion / release","text":"Adhesive: Magigoo PA, PVA glue; Raft / skirt / brim: Brim >10 mm / raft"}],"replaced":["nozzle","bed"]}],"replaced":[],"sources":[{"id":"D-FILLAMENTUM-NYLON-CF15-PAGE","publisher":"Fillamentum","title":"Nylon CF15 Carbon | Fillamentum","read":"2026-09-21","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"https://fillamentum.com/collections/nylon-filament/nylon-cf15-carbon-filament/","sha256":"035387e5b017e7ebf08186b0e840911354edd0a4fef8dc2b5286c23424700d74","note":"The maker's own product page, fetched as a witness in the V2 import (ledger, duplicate kind product-page); what it says is the maker's marketing text.","gave":{"measurements":3,"profiles":0,"statements":0,"environment":0,"resin":0,"guide":false},"products":["G154-01"]},{"id":"R-EMS-GRIVORY-RESISTANCE-TO-CHEMICALS","publisher":"EMS-GRIVORY","title":"Technical Data Sheet Grilon, Grilamid and Grivory – Resistance to Chemicals"